.TH PDFANNEX 1
.SH NAME
pdfannex \- prepare and verify reproducible PDF annex inputs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdfannex
.I command
[
.I document.tex
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdfannex
records requested annex sources, resolves external sources, and stores their
PDF bytes by SHA-256 so later builds can use the same inputs.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create an empty
.B pdfannex.lock
in the current directory. This opts the LaTeX package in to recording source
requests.
.TP
.B prepare document.tex
Resolve requested sources that are not already locked, then update the
resolution map. Does not contact resolvers if all sources are already locked.
.TP
.B update document.tex
Explicitly re-resolve all requested sources and advance the lock.
.TP
.B status document.tex
Report whether locked sources changed upstream. Resolver-backed sources may
contact their services.
.TP
.B verify document.tex
Check the lock, local artifact store, and resolution map without contacting
resolvers.
.SH RESOLVERS
Plain file paths are handled by
.B pdfannex
itself. Other source schemes require an executable named
.BR pdfannex-resolver-SCHEME
on
.BR PATH .
Resolvers run only for explicit CLI commands, never during LaTeX compilation.
Individual adapters may require external programs; consult their
documentation.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
The command is a TeXLua script and requires
.BR texlua ,
provided by TeX Live. On systems that do not add TeX Live scripts to
.BR PATH ,
invoke it with
.B texlua
and its installed script path, or add the scripts directory to
.BR PATH .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdflatex (1),
.BR texlua (1)
